WEBVTT

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.930
You did well, Baki.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.600
We're out of time!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.080
Defense, push up!

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.960
Keep your focus guys! Concentrate!

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.220
Our first win this season!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.970
Did you see that, Fuwa?!

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.210
Yes!!

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.830
Manager!

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:06.420
Uncle, do you still have a copy of Football Digest?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.060
Yeah, I think so.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.020
Found it!

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.330
I'm so excited!

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.400
How many times must I say?

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.680
Lower your volume!
Hurry up, Kota!

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.660
What's the rush?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.180
He looks so cool, Tsubaki!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.850
Tatsumi's in it too!

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.420
Nice job, cameraman!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.250
We have to buy this.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.450
It's the edition that includes Tatsumi's first win as ETU's manager.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.180
Let's gather our money and buy it!

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.490
Yeah!

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:44.740
Why are we always so poor?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.350
This isn't enough...

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.450
Hey, Goro's son.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:50.070
Huh?

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:56.450
You'll get to read it back at home. Your dad bought one just now.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.080
Huh? Really? Nice, old man!

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.030
I'm jealous...

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.990
But seriously, what's up with your dad?

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:10.590
Is this year's ETU that interesting?

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.860
He was so assertive in getting me to join.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.090
Let's do it, Takebo!

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.100
Let's revive the Edomae Army!

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.600
Look at this flag and this jersey!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.690
Remember that passion you once had!

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.610
After all, Tatsumi's the manager!

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.230
Even as a manager, he brings us the same excitement!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.410
You liked Tatsumi, too, right?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.990
Hey... Slow down, Goro.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.900
It does feel nostalgic...

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.730
but I haven't been to the stadium in 10 years, and I don't know any of the players.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.980
Then just start learning it now.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.090
There's this player called Tsubaki...

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.680
Hey, Goro...

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:01.010
Back then, we were young and had time to spare...

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:08.070
But now, I have to feed my family and my business isn't doing that well either.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.520
I just don't have the time to catch up with soccer anymore.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.890
Sorry.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.280
Goro.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.530
Shige...

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.190
I see, so luck isn't on your side either.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:34.060
Yeah, they all seem to have their own things to take care of.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.300
Yeah right, we're busy everyday, too!

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.130
Though I guess we're slacking off for today.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:53.110
Well, I guess it's hard to become an enthusiast again at our age.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:06:01.270
But, you know, soccer is just so exciting.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:07.080
I've never felt so satisfied for a long time.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.950
Yeah, me too!

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.960
Hahaha, we've become kinda creepy.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:20.840
I actually forgot how it felt like until Tatsumi came along.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:26.600
I'm sure they'll remember it all once they go to the stadium!

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:28.970
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.220
We can't give up! I'll try finding two or three more!

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.960
Me too!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.250
This is just the beginning!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.860
We're just getting started!

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.560
As PR, we need to seize this opportunity with both hands!

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:55.080
Oh, we're in the news. But our article is larger than I expected.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.690
Don't tell me you're satisfied with just this, chief.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.670
We're going to become even bigger...

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:08.260
And they will start to write even more about us in the future!

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.270
That would be nice.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.020
We can do it!

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:19.420
Furthermore, the team's morale hasn't been this good in years.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:25.410
The players' attitudes... Their aura as well...

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.630
They're totally different!

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.970
Oh, really?

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:41.020
We need to seize this opportunity to gain more fans!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.930
Right, I'm heading down to the training ground.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:46.930
Sure...

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.180
Kota, who are you getting an autograph from?

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:56.110
Hmm, how about you, Yoshio?

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:57.510
I want Tsubaki's!

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:02.070
What? Already? He'll get cocky.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.320
Then what about you?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.820
I've always been aiming for Prince's.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.870
He always just waves his hand and leaves. His autographs must be super rare!

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.510
Kota, what about you?

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.710
No... He's the manager!

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.140
So?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.800
I haven't decided.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.710
Just pick one already!

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:27.720
I know!

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.320
Huh? It's usually empty down here!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.280
Where did they come from?

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.480
Look, it's Tsubaki!

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:43.850
Yeah, it is!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.980
Tsubaki's fans!

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.890
The female ETU supporters used to be hardcore Prince fans...

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.490
Kuro, you're manly!

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.390
Kuroda fans...

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.500
They're as scary as ever.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.880
I guess winning changes everything.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:03.100
And they defeated a romping Nagoya.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.730
If we keep this up, the next win will come soon!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.260
Hey, too slow!

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.850
Didn't I say a maximum of two touches?

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.350
Move the ball around more. Let's use our heads, okay?

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:18.730
Hey, Prince!

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:21.850
Defenders, raise your voices! I can't hear you guys at all!

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.230
Go forth!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.730
Hey, how many times was that?

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.870
Left, left!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:28.570
Go.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.450
You're pressing too late!

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:35.580
You have to properly decide whether you're attacking or taking it slow!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.580
Run, run!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.670
That was a great chance!

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.890
You should have scored that!

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.180
That's tough...

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.580
I feel that they can make it this year...

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:02.510
Isn't this too much? Don't they have a match tomorrow?

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.170
What's the matter?

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:08.250
N-Nothing!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:12.450
Tomorrow's match is against Sapporo.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.670
We've already lost once against them.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:19.700
I have to push them hard so that the defeat won't creep into their head.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.370
We're still among the weakest.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.580
This is not the time to get complacent!

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.090
T-That's right...

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.160
I was getting complacent...

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.410
... just because we were featured in an article and have more practice spectators.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.060
Truth be told, we've only won once.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.470
I need to snap out of it!

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.730
Prince, stop lazing around!

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.970
This is kinda...

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.370
Let's get our autographs next time...

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.110
I guess it's just not the right time.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:04.450
We have to do something to improve Tatsumi's image!

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:12.310
We'll start a newsletter or a website to sell Tatsumi's plus points!

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:18.310
So, the content... Let's see...

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:20.670
Nagata...

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:25.270
You're working really hard, huh?

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:33.780
Though my daughter's an office lady, all she does is whine about her work.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:41.520
She doesn't save up too; always going on dates and vacations...

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:43.420
I see...

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:49.360
When I try to lecture her, she just says that she's making full use of her youth.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:56.080
And yet, you're about the same age as her and working hard in an environment like this.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.560
How I wish she's half as diligent as you.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.730
A pimple...

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.080
Maybe I really am working too hard.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.450
When was the last time I took a vacation?

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:22.670
But I have to work hard.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.830
I mean, the chief's still taking it easy...

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.850
And he still calls his workplace <i>"this environment"</i>...

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.340
Hiya, Yuri!

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.720
You're always so energetic, Sera.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.250
Oh, really?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:51.480
From the perspective of an ordinary girl, we could call it <i>"this environment"</i>.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:59.220
It kinda make sense now as to why I'm running out of topics to talk about with my office friends...

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:00.970
Still...

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:04.490
Oh, Sera, put your dirty clothes into the laundry immediately, okay?

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.800
Yes, Ma'am!

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.990
Ah, Midorikawa. The date for the interview has been set. I'll let you know later.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:15.000
Ok, thanks.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.130
Oh, right...

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:18.350
The autographed ball for the prize...

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:20.290
Hiya, Dori.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.100
Hey.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:21.660
The autographed ball for the prize...

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:21.760
You'll catch a cold like that.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.280
I need to get Murakoshi and...

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.680
It'll be fine!

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:37.400
Yuri?!

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:38.840
Get a hold of yourself!

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.880
She's dead! Dead!

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.400
How's that possible?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.880
Go to the infirmary and get the physio!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.020
O-Okay!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.880
Edomae army?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.420
That's right, for cheering during soccer games.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:06.390
I'm the one who needs some cheering. You haven't come in ages!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.310
I'm a bit busy lately...

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:12.720
Come on, have a drink.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.510
Maybe next time...

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:17.320
Hold on... Goro!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:27.700
Oh Mr. Fukazawa. What brings you here today?

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:31.210
Oh... Err...

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:34.860
So how's the TV I sent here a while ago?

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:41.420
Oh, DVB-T, right? Everyone was so excited! The graphics is great!

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.810
That's good to hear.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:48.470
I guess this is far too extreme...

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:52.630
I was just passing by, so I thought I'd check.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.480
Well, I'm off then.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:08.370
Ah, she's still alive.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.440
W-What are you doing?!

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:17.500
I came to get an ice-cream pop. There's no fridge in my room.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.380
Are you alright, Yuri?

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.630
You fainted.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.390
You must have been skipping meals and lacking sleep again.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:30.890
If you die, all your hard work will go to waste.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.790
Even if you did a good job, the result's still wasted.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.400
I see, I fainted...

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:40.910
You've been working non-stop since the start of the season.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:47.130
You need to take care of yourself, Yuri. If not, I'm going to get lectured by the chairman.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:52.160
Yes, I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.520
I will repay you by working...

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:55.840
No.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:59.970
Go home and rest for today. Now.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:03.370
But I'm fine now.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.050
That's not the point.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.870
If you stay and work,

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.680
everyone will be worried about you and they won't be able to concentrate.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.040
But...

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:17.530
Yeah, go home and get some rest, Yuri.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.070
Hurry up and go home!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.490
This is harder than I thought.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.060
Yeah.

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:35.710
Maybe we should just merge with the Skulls...

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.580
Over my dead body!

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.090
You're right.

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.490
They took my work away...

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:50.740
What's with everyone, ordering me to go home?

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.120
Sorry, I'm late.

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.240
It's okay.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:59.350
I'm sorry, my boss tried to give me overtime. I'm beat.

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.490
We should be about the same age.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:07.830
Office workers get off this early?

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:11.490
What's with the gap?

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.630
No, I guess it's normal.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:27.810
Still, it was fun watching Tatsumi during his playing days, right?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:32.300
Yeah, those were the exciting times.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:38.690
I lost count of the number of times my heart almost stopped beating due to that!

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.390
Yeah, me too.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:46.400
I'm sure Tatsumi will show us that brand of soccer again.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.830
That's right. And when they see that, our comrades will be sure to return!

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.020
Yeah!

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:58.410
Until then, we've got to build up a solid foundation, one that is able to beat the Skulls!

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.580
Yeah.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.820
All right...

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:05.780
Shall we get back to work, Goro? I don't want to be nagged at by my wife.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:08.050
Yeah.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:13.750
Wow, cherry blossoms. This reminds me of our first date.

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:15.300
Really?

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.600
Yes, don't you remember?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.980
So it reminds them of that...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.050
If it were me...

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.140
What're you trying to do?

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:43.080
Didn't they order you to go home and rest?

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:46.020
I'll do that after this.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.000
I'll eat and sleep to my heart's content.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:54.760
But before that, I need to take a photo of you and interview you for the newsletter.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:19:01.770
Why? Can't we do that tomorrow? Though it's already April, it's still freezing.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:06.630
I won't make anybody worry, since they all went home.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:10.530
And do you still remember?

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.090
Your debut match...

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:19.940
It was a night game, just like this.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:24.090
The cherry blossoms were also falling.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.850
That game, we were trailing 1-0...

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:47.330
But within 4 minutes of stoppage time, you managed to score two goals to seal a comeback win.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:20:01.980
Amongst the ETU fans, that legendary match was dubbed as "The Sumidagawa Miracle".

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.210
Really?

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:06.260
I figured you wouldn't remember.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.830
But you know, it will definitely help if the fans recall it...

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:20.620
And see you in that light when they see this picture.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.480
That's all your imagination.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:29.230
Yeah, I know. The strong ETU we once knew will be back.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.580
I can feel it.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.740
You must really love your job.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:47.250
The entire board will cheer when we score a goal.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:52.540
And when we're on a losing streak, it feels like you're attending a wake.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:59.750
It's the only workplace where you can feel so much passion.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.510
There's no place like this anywhere else.

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.820
So says the person who collapsed.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.190
T-That...

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:14.780
No player can sprint constantly for 90 minutes.

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:17.650
Balance is required for everything.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.790
If you're a footballer, that's the least you should know.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.480
It's freezing!

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:42.050
Look who's talking.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:52.410
Tsubaki, will you play well in the next one too?

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.900
Hey, you!

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.870
Why are you still grinning while you're reading that thing?

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:59.030
You should be working!

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:02.620
B-But we don't have any customers right now.

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:05.730
I'm talking about your attitude!

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:07.510
That's right, dad.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:10.040
You too, Kota?

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:13.050
The players are not having an easy time.

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.960
Don't be fooled!

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.690
What the?

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:20.840
Goro!

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:25.970
Yama from the photo lab agreed to join us!

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.100
Really?!

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:32.270
I have been interested for quite some time now...

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:34.360
Alright! Let's do it together!

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:35.190
Hey, you!

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:36.230
Dad!

00:22:36.230 --> 00:22:37.940
I just mentioned...

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:39.990
Don't be overly cheerful!

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:42.720
First, I'll teach you our chant!

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:43.850
Chant?

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:47.290
It's a cheer to support the team. The rhythm's very important.

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:49.130
Don't ignore us!

00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:16.790
Sera, substitution.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.840
Good job, Sera.

00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:22.460
Seems like Natsu's back.

00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:24.670
My name is Yotaro Natsuki.

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:28.220
I'll be joining ETU with immediate effect!
